{"id":"s4.4.1","slug":"fraction-subtraction-trick-supplement","title":"Additional Formulas: a/b - (na-1)/(nb-1)","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This is a supplement to the formulas in Section 1.5.5, dealing with specific forms of fraction subtraction. There are four variations in total, which are useful for quickly solving otherwise tedious problems.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Formulas:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>$\\frac{a}{b} - \\frac{na-1}{nb-1} = \\frac{b-a}{b(nb-1)}$</li><li>$\\frac{a}{b} - \\frac{na+1}{nb+1} = -\\frac{b-a}{b(nb+1)}$</li></ul><p>The key is to observe the numerator and denominator of the more complex fraction to see if they are one greater or one fewer than a multiple of the simpler fraction's numerator and denominator. This determines which formula to apply.</p>","summary":"This is a supplement to the formulas in Section 1.5.5, dealing with specific forms of fraction subtraction.","generation_guideline":"Generate a fraction subtraction problem that fits one of the specific forms, like a/b - (na-1)/(nb-1).","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{5}{7} - \\frac{9}{13}$.","answer":"2/91","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{5}{7} - \\frac{11}{15}$.","answer":"-2/105","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{7}{11} - \\frac{55}{87}$.","answer":"4/957","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{3}{5} - \\frac{59}{99}$.","answer":"2/495","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{2}{7} - \\frac{21}{71}$.","answer":"-5/497","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{29}{35} - \\frac{5}{6}$.","answer":"-1/210","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{43}{49} - \\frac{7}{8}$.","answer":"1/392","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{23}{25} - \\frac{229}{249}$.","answer":"2/6225","kind":"exact","tags":["fract